title expect paths carry the same escapes names do

# An expect path is a PATH, so it needs the same decoding a leaf
# does -- otherwise it could never match a decoded name, and the two
# would silently never meet. Its '/' separators are legitimate, so
# unlike a leaf there is no slash check and \057 simply decodes to
# one more separator.
#
# Conflict arguments are deliberately NOT decoded. A conflict kind is
# drawn from a closed vocabulary of five words, where an escape
# cannot make anything more expressible and could only admit new
# spellings of a word that has exactly one.
#
# The NUL case is not here yet. It is in devcheck/pending/.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: eq\075uals

expect quarantined /eq\075uals
expect quarantined /a\400b
expect quarantined /a\slash
